From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:29:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] spanned_source_text: let an embedder's store keep the source
 text
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A script's source text is close to half of what a compiled bundle
keeps, and its one reader is Function.prototype.toString. An embedder
with storage outside the heap (kitesurf: a page facet's SQLite) can
hold it instead, and give back only the span a toString asks for.

An embedder installs a CodeStore per thread. Source texts of scripts,
modules and direct evals at or over its min_bytes register weakly, and
ks_swap_source_texts, called at an idle point, hands the still-live
ones to the store, so a script that dies in its own eval never costs a
write. JSON.parse's transient text never registers. The text sits in a
RefCell and is read through map_code_points, so a swap skips a text
being read and is safe at any point. A refused put stays resident, a
failed read makes toString fall back to "[native code]", and dropping
a swapped text releases its key. The code counters gain swapped texts
and bytes, store reads and store failures.

beep-boop-🤖
